  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_c94970677b844011986b6c34aa1dac78",
      "statement": "Production stacks and the CI runner run as two separate rootless Docker daemons on the same homelab host, publishing into the same host port space, so a prod 0.0.0.0 bind collides with a CI bind on the same port number — and the collision manifests as a crash-loop on the losing side rather than a clean bind error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/prod-reboot-resilience.md#L96-L96",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9877b3772b966b7e63146d59ab3262a91c49756ebc7307ae46454fcf020bb158:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/check-prod-ci-port-collision.mjs#L2-L13",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:330fffb93cd014b56bfb0de52478310fd74c98e32db7fb8d8512bb93af77abcb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1265121f5d744cfeb07f1fc80e51f19b",
      "statement": "The convention reserves host ports 19000–19099 for prod admin/UI publishes; the three prod published ports are Keycloak admin 19099:8080, LangFuse web 19030:3000 and Grafana/otel-lgtm 19002:3000, and every other service in the prod composes is unpublished (reached by Docker DNS on shared networks).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/prod-reboot-resilience.md#L86-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:789369d3cb7c6f3917200b07a4021b7aa6c9b6c471fe6c3856a807c9f85ee277:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/keycloak/compose.prod.yaml#L45-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0e6c3cfc51950e9abe258258e6cf0961e4b42e8b888badc7710511a0e8d6a80e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/observability/compose.prod.yaml#L236-L243",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dc1eef13f9a246a59e7bb94d72e6e12b93d8846d6f9f1386858d2f0b925400ab:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/observability/compose.prod.yaml#L40-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3a8f5a4881ef5ea65781fc28b0ea0c3691c9755b74b6cc958f5d0faa7b01efd0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3ed24ae82fea45319e7f0599311cfe4e",
      "statement": "The prod admin/UI publishes bind 0.0.0.0 with a plain HOST:CONTAINER mapping rather than a tailnet-IP-scoped bind, because the rootless daemon starts before tailscaled at boot and a <tailnet-ip>:host:container publish silently fails; tailnet-only exposure is preserved solely by the host's default-deny-inbound firewall posture, which is load-bearing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/prod-reboot-resilience.md#L94-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7373daa643e774929c7552ffc8be34086a24552156dac62b3caa34bd1c22a12a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/keycloak/compose.prod.yaml#L46-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:03c3e7b5f1968b8159ae8dc2e5531ef40e3f869af1b323c08f1b11fd5ec7a705:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/observability/compose.prod.yaml#L9-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4aeafb227da2885197e08ab3db1ab703561a14cdbbe8b77e05eec786e6a65c05:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bad6163d94444b068d929f30f15cc94e",
      "statement": "scripts/check-prod-ci-port-collision.mjs classifies a compose file as prod when its basename ends .prod.yaml (under infrastructure-as-code/docker/**) and every other tracked compose file (compose.yaml, compose.ci.yaml, compose.agent-e2e.yaml, stacks/*.compose.yaml) as CI/dev, then fails the scan when a fixed host port appears in both sets.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/check-prod-ci-port-collision.mjs#L102-L127",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6bd7a6688e51eff82c967e028de1f1b303a6b964fa63ccf45ea88989c6a5f13c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/check-prod-ci-port-collision.mjs#L15-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dfe03652152df016a4654a699f6462bb811734714d94d9ef2eafc7bcb1d01c99:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b9ab79ced1814d7cb86695a427d9dea4",
      "statement": "The collision gate compares host port NUMBERS only: entries with no deterministic fixed host port are skipped (a bare container port, a ${VAR} host field, an unparseable entry), host_ip is ignored, and numeric host-port ranges are expanded.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/check-prod-ci-port-collision.mjs#L34-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e54763831f7df220dd54b8c4d25ae40ef92edb1511a54b0598a2f2b998cb35e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0d98456b2b854c44931fa10ac2ef9d03",
      "statement": "The collision gate exits 0 when clean or when its selftest passes, 1 on a collision or a broken selftest, and 2 on bad arguments or an unparseable compose file; --selftest plants an overlap on port 19099 and asserts the parser cases so a gate that stopped detecting cannot report green.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/check-prod-ci-port-collision.mjs#L157-L196",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bed4abd332b461ad0bfa074ce109b072dcc18b84b2c26e074fd6366d5db2a852:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/check-prod-ci-port-collision.mjs#L20-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cc4e2b6a82ac52e9dbd8917dcaa1a17558b860de17ea0ea58f94244f242cf100:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cbe4d3bc21cf4d458d26d3f2023a8176",
      "statement": "The prod↔CI port-collision gate is a required guardrail step: the naming job in .forgejo/workflows/guardrails.yml runs its --selftest and then the scan on every pull request and every push to main.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.forgejo/workflows/guardrails.yml#L121-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c1e5bf6d93cc54c9836e654437d89d56ee465aca70d750f3ebdba7fa95c9018f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://.forgejo/workflows/guardrails.yml#L51-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d4db3c4003f85c29dd0a5588c2dcb4f2d3c77909571fd2f5445a7d40bfb08adf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6221b79daa834106840685c5fc3da4e2",
      "statement": "scripts/preflight.mjs runs the same selftest-then-scan pair for the port-collision gate locally, so a collision is caught before it reaches CI.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/preflight.mjs#L31-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:caf1f04345333c672adb67dbaab4c29cfa477e1ada3cf60c3a0a325143852574:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_25a69b1eac1f443790ee8ce8ee94e0cc",
      "statement": "The 2026-07-06 prod-auth outage: feature 028 bound the prod Keycloak admin at 0.0.0.0:8099, which overlapped the CI app-e2e Keycloak's 127.0.0.1:8099; a leftover CI stack held the port for about six hours, prod Keycloak could not bind on redeploy, and prod auth crash-looped until prod admin ports moved into the reserved range.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/prod-reboot-resilience.md#L96-L96",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9877b3772b966b7e63146d59ab3262a91c49756ebc7307ae46454fcf020bb158:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/check-prod-ci-port-collision.mjs#L4-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:67595cf9e09cf8dd7b742f4c2a6ac896be6ad1766773e7a5dbcf85532565230a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_37601233ec524e8db80f487314af35d8",
      "statement": "Moving or adding a prod published port also requires updating that port's self-referencing URL var, because the collision gate only scans the compose ports: key — concretely KC_HOSTNAME_ADMIN in infrastructure-as-code/komodo/stacks.toml and LangFuse's own NEXTAUTH_URL login/callback URL in the observability prod compose.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/observability/compose.prod.yaml#L72-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48cdcff65aaf7b005e8e18475bfedff336869473a2be0d4608ed18960f6d4731:"
        },
        {
